{"uid":"modules/chain_loop.py","name":"chain_loop.py","qualname":"modules/chain_loop.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/chain_loop.py","line":1,"end_line":315,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Chain-aware loop execution: one contract, two transport modes.","description":"When the autonomous planner emits an ``apt_chain <chain> <target>``\ndecision, this module decides how the chain executes:\n\n- ``stepwise`` (default when eligible): a :class:`ChainRunner` runs the\n  chain in-process and every chain step is routed through the worker's\n  own :meth:`Worker._guard_step`, so each step inherits scope, deny,\n  OS-gate, OPSEC, detection, missing-tool and budget guardrails and is\n  recorded in the task traffic log individually. Per-step pacing comes\n  from the shared EdrPacer plus the step's own ``sleep``/``jitter``.\n- ``subprocess`` (fallback): the whole chain runs through the existing\n  shell verb path exactly as before; stepwise is refused when a step\n  is not loop-routable or a nested chain exceeds the depth budget.\n\nThe mode is chosen by ``payload.json -> orchestrator.chain_mode``\n(``auto`` default, or forced ``stepwise``/``subprocess``). Everything\nreuses existing contracts: ``chain_registry`` resolves, ``chain_runner``\nexecutes, ``chain_facts`` spools, ``chain_state`` names runs.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/chain_loop.py::CHAIN_COMMAND_PREFIX","modules/chain_loop.py::chain_mode","modules/chain_loop.py::is_chain_command","modules/chain_loop.py::parse_chain_invocation","modules/chain_loop.py::stepwise_eligible","modules/chain_loop.py::ChainStepBlocked","modules/chain_loop.py::run_chain_stepwise"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
